# Line-ending policy — keep every text file LF in the repo AND in the working
# tree on every OS.
#
# Why this exists: on Windows, Git's core.autocrlf default rewrites LF -> CRLF
# in the working tree on checkout. Biome's formatter expects LF (biome.json
# formatter.lineEnding defaults to lf), so a CRLF checkout flags every file with
# a stray carriage return and `pnpm run lint` fails on 1000+ files. `eol=lf`
# overrides core.autocrlf, so any Windows checkout (a local contributor, even
# though Windows is not in the CI matrix) sees the same LF as macOS/Linux.
#
# After changing this file, run `git add --renormalize .` once to apply it to
# already-tracked files.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize line endings, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.svg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wasm binary
*.gz binary
*.node binary
